@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Wall collision audio - Beat my track</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101b27;color:#e9e3d7;font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:860px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}h2,a{color:#ffd667}article{padding:22px;margin:18px 0;border:1px solid #344450;border-radius:12px;background:#182632}audio{width:100%}p,small{color:#b3bec5}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #344450}</style><main><h1>Wall collision onset</h1><p>The reproduced large gap came from the rendered bumper reaching the wall before the circular driving collider. At 4 m/s, compact visible touch was tick62, while the physical response was tick81:158ms. The sound now starts at tick62; the existing physical response stays at tick81. The later same-wall cue is deduplicated.</p><table><tr><th>Compact speed</th><th>Old geometry gap</th><th>New cue gap</th></tr><tr><td>11 km/h</td><td>216.7 ms</td><td>0.0 ms</td></tr><tr><td>14 km/h</td><td>158.3 ms</td><td>0.0 ms</td></tr><tr><td>18 km/h</td><td>125.0 ms</td><td>0.0 ms</td></tr><tr><td>36 km/h</td><td>58.3 ms</td><td>0.0 ms</td></tr><tr><td>90 km/h</td><td>25.0 ms</td><td>0.0 ms</td></tr></table><p>All25 forward cases/five cars align at visible touch. Actual Game callback: sound and visible touch both62, response81. No canonical handling/input/record change. The three collision files now begin at their strongest transient, with no leading silence or fade-in.</p><article><h2>Light contact</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="impact-0-output.wav"></audio><p>Actual protected desktop master output. First meaningful signal reaches half its peak within one48kHz sample; the retained final-output limiter adds about2.04ms.</p></article><article><h2>Medium contact</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="impact-1-output.wav"></audio><p>Actual protected desktop master output. First meaningful signal reaches half its peak within one48kHz sample; the retained final-output limiter adds about2.04ms.</p></article><article><h2>Hard contact</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="impact-2-output.wav"></audio><p>Actual protected desktop master output. First meaningful signal reaches half its peak within one48kHz sample; the retained final-output limiter adds about2.04ms.</p></article><small>Digital/source/dispatch evidence does not measure speaker/Bluetooth latency. WASAPI reports about10ms output latency. Device/owner listening remains open. Existing cleared qubodup/Nox source credits remain in the bank NOTICE/manifest; only the three impact derivatives changed.</small></main></html>
